Withdrawn 2026-08-31 before the runner was installed.

The operator was already running this exact re-gate by hand. Installing the
runner with this job still queued would have run it a SECOND time, minutes
later, and spent the $2.18 twice — on the same page, for the same answer.

The runner's own guard does not cover this: it claims a job before running so
two launchd ticks cannot both start it, but a job queued here and a person
running the same command in a terminal are two different launch paths, and
nothing reconciles them. Worth remembering the next time a job is queued for
something a human may already be doing.
